Representative rendering-test coverage
======================================

Status and objective
  In progress. The user approved representative behavior and failure-mode coverage on
  2026-11-03, including explicit loss of exhaustive parameter combinations. The target is
  a complete correctness run below five minutes, excluding builds. On 2026-11-04 the user clarified
  that this means routine runs with validated shader caches retained; explicit uncached mechanics
  checks must remain. Cold-start results are reported separately. The target is not yet demonstrated.
  Process splitting is excluded from this work.
  Planned follow-up is Phase 11 in Rendering.TestRuntimeOptimizations.todo: bound geometry-fixture
  payload retention, attribute its possible contribution to GC cost, eliminate unused AO setup,
  qualify broader numerical executable reuse and assess authored blue-noise policy inputs.
  The candidates are unimplemented; reset/ownership proof and coverage agreements remain required.
  No runtime saving or five-minute outcome is established by the plan.
  Phase 10 in Rendering.TestRuntimeOptimizations.todo is complete and accepted by the user on
  2026-11-05, including its no-change dispositions and measured limitations. Its three-file test-source
  batch has clean second review and independent completion audit. Frame/wait and directional
  mechanisms remain; an atmosphere provider seam is deferred. The user approved ordinary debug
  demand preparing only lumon_combine per generation, losing full-catalog/debug coexistence there
  while retaining the complete registration witness and diagnostic workload. Sky-floor comparison
  keeps every original texel/value while reducing post-bounce reads from 512 to eight.
  Debug/Release each pass 75 distinct scoped checks, zero failures/skips. Full retained-cache
  Release passes 5,950 with six retained skips and zero failures in 435.814s (7m15.8s), excluding
  builds; all 5,956 runtime names and name/ID associations match Phase 9, with reconciled
  source/DLL/shader/cache stability.
  Original TRX parsing resolves wrapper metadata naming/Unicode defects without rerunning tests.
  The former conditional profiling-counter skip passes; no new skips or case removals occur.
  This single full result is slightly slower than Phase 9's 434.103s and shows no overall runtime
  improvement. The routine five-minute target remains unmet. Temporary sources are restored;
  the unchanged stress body attributed 21.256s of its 21.359s to GC.Collect in full-suite context.
  Detailed decisions, approved coverage loss, provenance and limitations are recorded in Phase 10;
  ../TestResults/TestRuntimeOptimizations/Phase10/20261105T1845Z/.
  Phases 1–10 are closed; the broader routine five-minute target remains open.
  On 2026-11-04 the user additionally approved replacing per-production SPIR-V admission
  matrices with focused mechanics tests. The last full Debug run, before this additional
  removal, took 732.960s: 6,620 passed, zero failed and seven skipped across 6,627 rows.
  The six accepted optimizations in Rendering.TestRuntimeOptimizations.todo remain closed.
  Phase 7 in that tasklist implements 40 additional case removals and four
  representative native water preparations while retaining all eight option-plan checks.
  The accepted Phase 7 Debug/Release full runs took 656.545s / 644.030s, excluding builds; each had
  5,975 passed, zero failed and seven skipped across 5,982 rows. Review and independent audit
  are clean; the user accepted Phase 7 on 2026-11-04. The under-five-minute objective is still unmet.
  The explicit keep/drop mapping and coverage losses are maintained there.
  Phase 8 in that tasklist implements a further 30-case reduction across installed PBR,
  terrain, scene-color, shared tracing and fallback commit coverage. Fresh discovery is 5,946
  per configuration (30 removed, zero added); focused Debug/Release each pass 122/122 with no
