Baseline and authority
  Current full Windows runs use AllTests.runsettings (Purpose!=Diagnostic, including stress).
  Debug: 872.548s wall, 7,015 passed / one failed / six skipped.
  Release: 953.882s wall, 7,016 passed / zero failed / six skipped.
  Both produce 7,022 runtime result rows; dynamic Poisson theories add six rows beyond the
  7,016 discovery identities. Debug's snapshot-startup timeout is retained as a failure,
  not silently excluded. Sources, DLLs and SPIR-V were stable during these measurements.
  Receipts: ../TestResults/TestRuntimeOptimizations/full-suite-current/20261104T053712Z/.
  Method ranking: ../TestResults/TestRuntimeOptimizations/five-minute-investigation/
  coverage-review/method-costs.csv. Summed case durations can overlap and are not wall savings.
  Current independent CPU collections already use xUnit parallel execution. GPU collection
  concurrency requires isolation of shared rendering services; no such change is included.
  The cancelled four-process trial supplies no valid timing or qualification evidence.

  Applicable sources:
  - GPU.IntegrationTestPerformance.Analysis.md and GPU.IntegrationTestPerformance.RemainingCosts.md:
    preserve independent references, ownership, meaningful lifecycle paths and honest measurement.
  - PBR.WaterRefraction.md and PBR.Liquids.md: public optical/fallback behavior, bounded traversal,
    signed projection, scene composition, continuity and material compatibility.
  - Current shader contracts and focused loading/ownership tests: preserve generic mechanics and
    their failure paths. Functional rendering tests own feature-specific numerical behavior.
    Per-production shader driver admission is intentionally no longer a separate inventory guarantee.

Implementation constraints
  Remove unneeded scenarios and repeated combinations; do not merely hide the same work in fewer
  wrappers. Preserve each required behavior and failure mode through a named surviving witness.
  Retained numerical references, tolerances and motion sweeps remain intact. No production shader,
  resource ownership, readiness condition, default selection or stress-workload change is included.
  Record exact removed identities and intentional coverage losses. Use configured test writers and
  independent test review; delegate builds/tests. Finish the related source batch before verification.

☑ Shader loading mechanics and installed-shader representatives
  Replace the 247-row compute and 35-row graphics inventory sweeps with two fixture-only tests:
  successful specialization/linking from a guarded unaligned slice without backing-buffer mutation,
  and three compute-asset generations with old-facade re-disposal after the new owner exists.
  Retain native program/pipeline readiness, deletion, idempotent disposal and GL-error assertions.
  Remove the 324-row generic runtime assignment matrix. Keep its seven dedicated lifecycle/failure
  cases, including raw SPIR-V graphics drawing, invalid replacement and uniform-dictionary checks.
  Remove the now-unused pairwise-selector helper and registry-enumeration infrastructure.
  Intentional loss: independent native-driver admission for production shader identities and
  assignments. Focused settings, stage plans, binary/metadata validation, specialization, execution,
  bindings, reload and ownership tests remain; numerical feature tests still use real shaders.
  The successful guarded-slice and old-compute-facade controls have no exact focused substitutes
  elsewhere, so they remain rather than deleting the inventory class's guarantees wholesale.
  Installed PBR: 60 -> 36 linking variants; its 12 other cases remain. Keep all five mesh families
  in both lighting modes, shadow endpoints 0/2, an intermediate shadow-1 witness, the conditional
  entity OIT-on branch, each family's SSAO/SSBO/depth-off case and the high-shadow standard case.
  Its intentional loss is the installed-source shadow/OIT/lighting cross-product coverage.
  No claim is made that an omitted production assignment can never reveal a defect.
  Superseded intermediate selection: runtime 480 -> 324 and compute 372 -> 247 retained all
  identities, option values and valid option pairs. That selection was built and independently
  verified in both configurations before the user approved removing the admission sweeps.
  Prototype estimates of 268/153 were superseded by actual compiled counts; they are not evidence.

☑ Water behavior representatives
  Production composition: 95 -> 33 rows. Keep baseline scenarios 0..14, 16 and 17; add three
  scenario-0 full-size quality-0/1/2 rows, one high-quality half-size row, scene-linear scenarios
  0/9/14, both nondefault scattering sources for scene 9, all five material compatibility cases,
  and both quality-0 captured-receiver sizes. Keep all four quality selections in real composition.
  Diagnostic traversal: 14 -> one positive-view-Z ray, scenario 8 / budget 8 / full source.
  Budget 17, continuity seven, filter 20, UV 37, pixel-normal 12 and reducer six remain unchanged.
  Surviving production, budget, continuity, filter, UV and reducer witnesses cover the removed
  fallback, invalid-source, bounded-work, edge and grazing behaviors. The signed geometric ray
  retains its direct positive-view-Z assertion.
  Intentional loss: most scene/quality/resolution/lighting-source cross-products, three intermediate
  camera combinations, and standalone diagnostic reason-code/read-counter oracles except where
  counters establish required loop ceilings, fallback reuse and zero-lookup TIR behavior.

☑ Surface and cloud overlap
  Surface families: 41 -> 26 rows. Consumer runtime retains all 13 rows, including all CPU/GPU x
  gather-mode startup rows and both directional-budget backends. Dedicated numerical checks for
  both gather implementations remain unchanged.
  Scenarios: 12 -> four. Keep emission-only and doorway transitions in SH0, progressive bounce
  and unavailable-versus-dark geometry in SH9. Retire the indirect-only retained-source and
  dark-replacement methods after transferring their unique intermediate-output/confidence
  assertions into the stronger numerical PBR lifetime witnesses.
  Spatial: ten -> six. Keep SH0 camera alignment and signed streaming, SH9 ring overlap and
  sealed-neighbor movement, and both mixed-consumer regression/control rows.
  PBR lifetime: six -> three. Keep SH0 source restoration and sealed-neighbor composition, SH9
  cache replacement. Preserve independent numerical composition, direct snapshots and lifetime
  checks; transfer the removed scenarios' boundary observations at matching indirect states.
  Cloud publication retains its existing Fact but samples complete solutions at profiles 0/2/4
  (endpoints/default), rather than all five. Keep all five quality mappings and actual direction
  budgets in their owning tests, and the independent density CPU oracle remains unchanged.
  Intentional loss: each shared transition crossed with both gather modes, and complete-solution
  publication smoke at cloud profiles 1/3. Every retained profile keeps its update/publication work.

